IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `s121-nouns`
IMPORT `s121-support`
IMPORT `s121-a-exclusion`
IMPORT `s121-b-limitations`
IMPORT `s121-c-reduced`
IMPORT `s121-d1-special`
IMPORT `s121-d9-service`
IMPORT `s121-efg`
IMPORT `s121-whole`
IMPORT `s121-seat`

-- INDEPENDENT TESTS for 26 U.S.C. section 121.
-- Every expected value below is from ANSWERS.md, written from the text before any .l4 file was opened.
-- Scenario numbers are the numbers of ANSWERS.md.
-- Where a day count could move an amount by a few hundred dollars the assertion uses `near` with a tolerance, and says so. These are differences by reading, not noise: each such line says which reading, with both amounts, and an exact assertion P-Sn at the end of the file shows the encoding returning the reader's amount for the reader's day count.
-- GAPS (no function can be asked): S11 S28 S29 S53 S107 S109 S110 S111 S112 S113 S114 S115 S130.

§ `Helpers (not assertions)`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
iso MEANS Date d m y

GIVEN y1 IS A NUMBER
      m1 IS A NUMBER
      d1 IS A NUMBER
      y2 IS A NUMBER
      m2 IS A NUMBER
      d2 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Span
sp MEANS Span OF (Date d1 m1 y1), (Date d2 m2 y2)

GIVETH A DATE
sale23 MEANS Date 30 6 2023

GIVETH A DATE
d1900 MEANS Date 1 1 1900

GIVETH A Holding
nohold MEANS Holding OF EMPTY, EMPTY

GIVETH A LIST OF Span
base19 MEANS LIST (sp 2019 1 1 2023 6 30)

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      target IS A NUMBER
      tol IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
near MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST x THEN (x AT LEAST (target MINUS tol)) AND (x AT MOST (target PLUS tol))

GIVEN f IS A `Sale facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
gainOut MEANS `s 121 the amount of the gain excluded from gross income` f

-- A single filer: the sale date, the gain, the periods owned, the periods used as the principal residence, the dates of earlier sales to which (a) applied.
GIVEN sale IS A DATE
      gain IS A NUMBER
      own IS A LIST OF Span
      use IS A LIST OF Span
      other IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A `Sale facts`
solo MEANS `the usual facts of a sale of a home` sale gain FALSE (`an individual who only owned and used the property` own use other) `no spouse` EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- A single filer with the three reasons of (c)(2)(B).
GIVEN sale IS A DATE
      gain IS A NUMBER
      own IS A LIST OF Span
      use IS A LIST OF Span
      other IS A LIST OF DATE
      employment IS A BOOLEAN
      health IS A BOOLEAN
      unforeseen IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Sale facts`
soloR MEANS `the usual facts of a sale of a home` sale gain FALSE (`an individual who only owned and used the property` own use other) `no spouse` EMPTY employment health unforeseen

-- A single filer with depreciation adjustments.
GIVEN sale IS A DATE
      gain IS A NUMBER
      own IS A LIST OF Span
      use IS A LIST OF Span
      adjustments IS A LIST OF `Depreciation adjustment`
GIVETH A `Sale facts`
soloD MEANS `the usual facts of a sale of a home` sale gain FALSE (`an individual who only owned and used the property` own use EMPTY) `no spouse` adjustments FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- A single filer whose taxpayer record is built elsewhere.
GIVEN sale IS A DATE
      gain IS A NUMBER
      taxpayer IS AN `Individual facts`
GIVETH A `Sale facts`
soloT MEANS `the usual facts of a sale of a home` sale gain FALSE taxpayer `no spouse` EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- A joint return.
GIVEN sale IS A DATE
      gain IS A NUMBER
      taxpayer IS AN `Individual facts`
      spouse IS AN `Individual facts`
GIVETH A `Sale facts`
jointF MEANS `the usual facts of a sale of a home` sale gain TRUE taxpayer spouse EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- A single filer with temporary absences.
GIVEN sale IS A DATE
      gain IS A NUMBER
      own IS A LIST OF Span
      use IS A LIST OF Span
      absences IS A LIST OF `Temporary absence`
GIVETH A `Sale facts`
soloAbs MEANS `the facts of a sale` sale `sale or exchange` gain FALSE (`an individual who only owned and used the property` own use EMPTY) `no spouse` EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE d1900 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY absences FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- A single filer with periods a spouse or former spouse used the home.
GIVEN sale IS A DATE
      gain IS A NUMBER
      own IS A LIST OF Span
      use IS A LIST OF Span
      spouseUse IS A LIST OF Span
GIVETH A `Sale facts`
soloSp MEANS `the facts of a sale` sale `sale or exchange` gain FALSE (`an individual who only owned and used the property` own use EMPTY) `no spouse` spouseUse FALSE FALSE FALSE d1900 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- The gates: event, (f), (d)(10), (d)(8). The gain is 100,000.
GIVEN sale IS A DATE
      event IS AN `Event in respect of the property`
      taxpayer IS AN `Individual facts`
      elects IS A BOOLEAN
      likekind IS A BOOLEAN
      seller IS A BOOLEAN
      acq IS A DATE
      remainder IS A BOOLEAN
      electsRem IS A BOOLEAN
      another IS A BOOLEAN
      related IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Sale facts`
gated MEANS `the facts of a sale` sale event 100000 FALSE taxpayer `no spouse` EMPTY elects likekind seller acq remainder electsRem another related EMPTY EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN amt IS A NUMBER
      per IS A Span
GIVETH A LIST OF `Depreciation adjustment`
dep MEANS LIST `Depreciation adjustment` WITH
    `amount` IS amt
    `period it is attributable to` IS per

GIVEN per IS A Span
GIVETH A LIST OF `Temporary absence`
absEmp MEANS LIST `Temporary absence` WITH
    `days` IS per
    `change of employment` IS TRUE
    `health conditions` IS FALSE
    `unforeseen circumstances as may be specified by the Secretary` IS FALSE

GIVEN decree IS A BOOLEAN
      incident IS A BOOLEAN
      sep IS A BOOLEAN
      support IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Instrument
instr MEANS Instrument WITH
    `a decree of divorce or separate maintenance` IS decree
    `a written instrument incident to such a decree` IS incident
    `a written separation agreement` IS sep
    `a decree requiring a spouse to make payments for the support or maintenance of the other spouse` IS support

GIVEN per IS A Span
      inst IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A LIST OF `Use granted`
grant MEANS LIST `Use granted` WITH
    `days` IS per
    `instrument` IS inst

GIVEN per IS A Span
      lic IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Stay in a facility`
stay MEANS LIST `Stay in a facility` WITH
    `days` IS per
    `facility licensed by a State or political subdivision to care for an individual in the taxpayer's condition` IS lic

-- A period of service as a member of the uniformed services: the span, the miles to the duty station, residing in Government quarters, then the call.
GIVEN per IS A Span
      miles IS A NUMBER
      quarters IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Period of service`
uniSvc MEANS `Period of service` WITH
    `days` IS per
    `capacity` IS `member of the uniformed services`
    `serving outside the United States` IS FALSE
    `miles from the duty station to the property` IS miles
    `residing under Government orders in Government quarters` IS quarters
    `on active duty pursuant to a call or order` IS TRUE
    `days the call or order is for` IS 0
    `the call or order is for an indefinite period` IS TRUE
    `a member of the uniformed services under section 101(a)(5) of title 10` IS TRUE
    `a member of the Service under section 103(1) to (5) of the Foreign Service Act of 1980` IS FALSE
    `an employee as defined by section 2105 of title 5` IS FALSE
    `office of the intelligence community` IS `some other office`
    `an enrolled volunteer under section 5 of the Peace Corps Act` IS FALSE
    `a volunteer leader under section 6 of the Peace Corps Act` IS FALSE

-- A call to active duty: the number of days it is for, and whether it is for an indefinite period.
GIVEN per IS A Span
      callDays IS A NUMBER
      indefinite IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Period of service`
svcCall MEANS `Period of service` WITH
    `days` IS per
    `capacity` IS `member of the uniformed services`
    `serving outside the United States` IS FALSE
    `miles from the duty station to the property` IS 200
    `residing under Government orders in Government quarters` IS FALSE
    `on active duty pursuant to a call or order` IS TRUE
    `days the call or order is for` IS callDays
    `the call or order is for an indefinite period` IS indefinite
    `a member of the uniformed services under section 101(a)(5) of title 10` IS TRUE
    `a member of the Service under section 103(1) to (5) of the Foreign Service Act of 1980` IS FALSE
    `an employee as defined by section 2105 of title 5` IS FALSE
    `office of the intelligence community` IS `some other office`
    `an enrolled volunteer under section 5 of the Peace Corps Act` IS FALSE
    `a volunteer leader under section 6 of the Peace Corps Act` IS FALSE

-- A period of service as an employee, for a given office.
GIVEN per IS A Span
      office IS AN `Office of the intelligence community`
GIVETH A `Period of service`
svcOffice MEANS `Period of service` WITH
    `days` IS per
    `capacity` IS `employee of the intelligence community`
    `serving outside the United States` IS FALSE
    `miles from the duty station to the property` IS 200
    `residing under Government orders in Government quarters` IS FALSE
    `on active duty pursuant to a call or order` IS TRUE
    `days the call or order is for` IS 0
    `the call or order is for an indefinite period` IS TRUE
    `a member of the uniformed services under section 101(a)(5) of title 10` IS FALSE
    `a member of the Service under section 103(1) to (5) of the Foreign Service Act of 1980` IS FALSE
    `an employee as defined by section 2105 of title 5` IS TRUE
    `office of the intelligence community` IS office
    `an enrolled volunteer under section 5 of the Peace Corps Act` IS FALSE
    `a volunteer leader under section 6 of the Peace Corps Act` IS FALSE

-- A Peace Corps enrolled volunteer, serving outside the United States or not.
GIVEN per IS A Span
      outside IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Period of service`
pcSvc MEANS `Period of service` WITH
    `days` IS per
    `capacity` IS `enrolled volunteer or volunteer leader under the Peace Corps Act`
    `serving outside the United States` IS outside
    `miles from the duty station to the property` IS 0
    `residing under Government orders in Government quarters` IS FALSE
    `on active duty pursuant to a call or order` IS FALSE
    `days the call or order is for` IS 0
    `the call or order is for an indefinite period` IS FALSE
    `a member of the uniformed services under section 101(a)(5) of title 10` IS FALSE
    `a member of the Service under section 103(1) to (5) of the Foreign Service Act of 1980` IS FALSE
    `an employee as defined by section 2105 of title 5` IS FALSE
    `office of the intelligence community` IS `some other office`
    `an enrolled volunteer under section 5 of the Peace Corps Act` IS TRUE
    `a volunteer leader under section 6 of the Peace Corps Act` IS FALSE

-- Individuals with one special family of facts each. Positional: see `Individual facts` in s121-whole.l4.
GIVEN own IS A LIST OF Span
      use IS A LIST OF Span
      services IS A LIST OF `Period of service`
      elects IS A BOOLEAN
      other IS A BOOLEAN
      revoked IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Individual facts`
indSvc MEANS `the facts of an individual` (Holding OF own, use) FALSE nohold d1900 EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE nohold FALSE EMPTY FALSE 0 services elects other revoked EMPTY FALSE

GIVEN own IS A LIST OF Span
      use IS A LIST OF Span
      other IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH AN `Individual facts`
indOther MEANS `an individual who only owned and used the property` own use other

GIVEN own IS A LIST OF Span
      use IS A LIST OF Span
      transferor IS A LIST OF Span
GIVETH AN `Individual facts`
ind1041 MEANS `the facts of an individual` (Holding OF own, use) FALSE nohold d1900 EMPTY TRUE transferor EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE nohold FALSE EMPTY FALSE 0 EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE

GIVEN own IS A LIST OF Span
      use IS A LIST OF Span
      grants IS A LIST OF `Use granted`
GIVETH AN `Individual facts`
indGrant MEANS `the facts of an individual` (Holding OF own, use) FALSE nohold d1900 EMPTY FALSE EMPTY grants FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE nohold FALSE EMPTY FALSE 0 EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE

GIVEN own IS A LIST OF Span
      use IS A LIST OF Span
      stock IS A LIST OF Span
      occupy IS A LIST OF Span
GIVETH AN `Individual facts`
indCoop MEANS `the facts of an individual` (Holding OF own, use) FALSE nohold d1900 EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY TRUE stock occupy FALSE nohold FALSE EMPTY FALSE 0 EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE

GIVEN own IS A LIST OF Span
      use IS A LIST OF Span
      converted IS A Holding
GIVETH AN `Individual facts`
indConv MEANS `the facts of an individual` (Holding OF own, use) FALSE nohold d1900 EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY TRUE converted FALSE EMPTY FALSE 0 EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE

GIVEN own IS A LIST OF Span
      use IS A LIST OF Span
      incap IS A BOOLEAN
      stays IS A LIST OF `Stay in a facility`
GIVETH AN `Individual facts`
indCare MEANS `the facts of an individual` (Holding OF own, use) FALSE nohold d1900 EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE nohold incap stays FALSE 0 EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE

GIVEN own IS A LIST OF Span
      use IS A LIST OF Span
      roll IS A BOOLEAN
      rollDays IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Individual facts`
indRoll MEANS `the facts of an individual` (Holding OF own, use) FALSE nohold d1900 EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE nohold FALSE EMPTY roll rollDays EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY FALSE

GIVEN own IS A LIST OF Span
      use IS A LIST OF Span
      f877 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Individual facts`
ind877 MEANS `the facts of an individual` (Holding OF own, use) FALSE nohold d1900 EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE EMPTY EMPTY FALSE nohold FALSE EMPTY FALSE 0 EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE EMPTY f877

-- A surviving spouse who owned and used the home from 2013-06-30; the late spouse did the same to the date of death.
GIVEN death IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Individual facts`
survTen MEANS `a surviving spouse who owned and used the property` (LIST (Span OF (Date 30 6 2013), sale23)) (LIST (Span OF (Date 30 6 2013), sale23)) EMPTY (Holding OF (LIST (Span OF (Date 30 6 2013), death)), (LIST (Span OF (Date 30 6 2013), death))) death EMPTY

§ `Subsection (a): the two-year-in-five test`

#ASSERT gainOut (solo sale23 100000 base19 base19 EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 100000 -- S1 (a): BASE, gain 100,000, owned and used 4.5 years => 100,000
#ASSERT gainOut (solo sale23 100000 (LIST (sp 2021 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2021 6 30 2023 6 30)) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 100000 -- S2 (a): 2 years and 1 day => 100,000
#ASSERT gainOut (solo sale23 100000 (LIST (sp 2021 7 1 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2021 7 1 2023 6 30)) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 100000 -- S3 (a): exactly 2 years counted inclusively => 100,000 (day-count sensitive)
#ASSERT gainOut (solo sale23 100000 (LIST (sp 2021 7 2 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2021 7 2 2023 6 30)) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 0 -- S4 (a): 2 years less 1 day => 0, Guide: "if" condition unmet
#ASSERT gainOut (solo sale23 100000 (LIST (sp 2012 1 1 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2012 1 1 2018 1 1)) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 0 -- S5 (a): use ended before the 5-year window => 0, Guide: "if"
-- WITHDRAWN 2026-11-18, SCENARIO (the reader's own mistake, see its triage; replaced by R6, which passes): #ASSERT gainOut (solo sale23 100000 (LIST (sp 2018 1 1 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2018 12 1 2019 12 1), (sp 2022 6 30 2023 6 30)) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 100000 -- S6 (a): two separate years of use aggregate to 2 years => 100,000
#ASSERT gainOut (solo sale23 100000 (LIST (sp 2017 1 1 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2017 1 1 2019 1 1)) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 0 -- S7 (a): only 0.5 year of the use is inside the window => 0, Guide: "if"
#ASSERT gainOut (solo sale23 100000 (LIST (sp 2017 6 30 2023 6 30)) EMPTY EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 0 -- S8 (a): never lived in it => 0, Guide: "if"
#ASSERT gainOut (solo sale23 100000 (LIST (sp 2018 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2021 12 30 2023 6 30)) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 0 -- S9 (a): used only 1.5 years => 0, Guide: "if"
#ASSERT gainOut (solo sale23 100000 (LIST (sp 2021 12 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2021 12 30 2023 6 30)) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 0 -- S10 (a): owned and used only 1.5 years => 0, Guide: "if"

§ `Subsection (b)(1): the ceiling`

#ASSERT gainOut (solo sale23 250000 base19 base19 EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 250000 -- S12 (b)(1): gain equal to the ceiling => 250,000
#ASSERT gainOut (solo sale23 250001 base19 base19 EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 250000 -- S13 (b)(1): gain one dollar over => 250,000
#ASSERT gainOut (solo sale23 600000 base19 base19 EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 250000 -- S14 (b)(1): gain 600,000 => 250,000

§ `Subsection (b)(2) and (d)(1): joint returns`

#ASSERT gainOut (jointF sale23 600000 (indOther (LIST (sp 2018 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2018 6 30 2023 6 30)) EMPTY) (indOther EMPTY (LIST (sp 2021 1 1 2023 6 30)) EMPTY)) EQUALS JUST 500000 -- S15 (b)(2)(A): husband owned and used 5 years, wife used 2.5 years, gain 600,000 => 500,000
#ASSERT gainOut (jointF sale23 500001 (indOther (LIST (sp 2018 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2018 6 30 2023 6 30)) EMPTY) (indOther EMPTY (LIST (sp 2021 1 1 2023 6 30)) EMPTY)) EQUALS JUST 500000 -- S16 (b)(2)(A): gain 500,001 => 500,000
#ASSERT gainOut (jointF sale23 400000 (indOther (LIST (sp 2018 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2018 6 30 2023 6 30)) EMPTY) (indOther EMPTY (LIST (sp 2021 1 1 2023 6 30)) EMPTY)) EQUALS JUST 400000 -- S17 (b)(2)(A): gain 400,000 => 400,000
#ASSERT gainOut (jointF sale23 400000 (indOther (LIST (sp 2018 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2018 6 30 2023 6 30)) EMPTY) (indOther EMPTY (LIST (sp 2022 6 30 2023 6 30)) EMPTY)) EQUALS JUST 250000 -- S18 (b)(2)(B): wife used only 1 year => 250,000
#ASSERT gainOut (jointF sale23 400000 (indOther (LIST (sp 2020 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2020 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (iso 2022 6 30))) (indOther (LIST (sp 2020 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2020 6 30 2023 6 30)) EMPTY)) EQUALS JUST 250000 -- S19 (b)(2)(B): husband barred by (b)(3), wife not => 250,000
#ASSERT gainOut (jointF sale23 400000 (indOther (LIST (sp 2020 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2020 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (iso 2022 6 30))) (indOther (LIST (sp 2020 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2020 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (iso 2022 6 30)))) EQUALS JUST 0 -- S20 (b)(2)(B): both spouses barred by (b)(3) => 0
#ASSERT gainOut (solo sale23 300000 (LIST (sp 2018 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2018 6 30 2023 6 30)) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 250000 -- S21 (b)(2): married filing separately, husband qualifies => 250,000 under (b)(1)
#ASSERT gainOut (jointF sale23 100000 (indOther (LIST (sp 2018 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2018 6 30 2023 6 30)) EMPTY) (indOther EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY)) EQUALS JUST 100000 -- S22 (d)(1): joint return, husband qualifies, wife never lived there => 100,000
#ASSERT gainOut (jointF sale23 80000 (indOther (LIST (sp 2022 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2022 6 30 2023 6 30)) EMPTY) (indOther (LIST (sp 2022 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2022 6 30 2023 6 30)) EMPTY)) EQUALS JUST 0 -- S23 (d)(1): joint return, neither spouse used 2 years, no (c) reason => 0, Guide: "if"

§ `Subsection (b)(3): one sale every two years`

#ASSERT gainOut (solo sale23 100000 base19 base19 (LIST (iso 2022 6 30))) EQUALS JUST 0 -- S24 (b)(3): earlier (a)-sale 12 months before => (a) does not apply => 0, Guide: flat negative "shall not apply"
#ASSERT gainOut (solo sale23 100000 base19 base19 (LIST (iso 2021 4 30))) EQUALS JUST 100000 -- S25 (b)(3): earlier (a)-sale 2 years 2 months before => no bar => 100,000
#ASSERT gainOut (solo sale23 100000 base19 base19 (LIST (iso 2021 7 1))) EQUALS JUST 0 -- S26 (b)(3): earlier (a)-sale on the first day of the 2-year period => barred => 0 (day-count sensitive)
#ASSERT gainOut (solo sale23 100000 base19 base19 (LIST (iso 2021 6 30))) EQUALS JUST 100000 -- S27 (b)(3): earlier (a)-sale the day before the 2-year period => no bar => 100,000 (day-count sensitive)

§ `Subsection (b)(4) and (d)(2): surviving spouse and a deceased spouse's period`

#ASSERT gainOut (soloT sale23 450000 (survTen (iso 2022 3 10))) EQUALS JUST 450000 -- S30 (b)(4): survivor, sale 15 months after death, requirements met => limit 500,000 => 450,000
#ASSERT gainOut (soloT sale23 450000 (survTen (iso 2021 6 30))) EQUALS JUST 450000 -- S31 (b)(4): sale exactly 2 years after death => limit 500,000 => 450,000
#ASSERT gainOut (soloT sale23 450000 (survTen (iso 2021 6 29))) EQUALS JUST 250000 -- S32 (b)(4): sale 2 years and 1 day after death => limit 250,000, Guide: period fixed in the text's own words
#ASSERT gainOut (solo sale23 450000 (LIST (sp 2013 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2013 6 30 2023 6 30)) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 250000 -- S33 (b)(4): survivor remarried before the sale, files separately => 250,000
#ASSERT gainOut (soloT sale23 400000 (`a surviving spouse who owned and used the property` EMPTY (LIST (sp 2021 12 30 2023 6 30)) EMPTY (Holding OF (LIST (sp 2013 6 30 2022 12 30)), (LIST (sp 2013 6 30 2022 12 30))) (iso 2022 12 30) EMPTY)) EQUALS JUST 250000 -- S34 (b)(4): survivor had lived there only 1 year when the spouse died => 250,000
#ASSERT gainOut (soloT sale23 100000 (`a surviving spouse who owned and used the property` (LIST (sp 2022 7 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2022 7 30 2023 6 30)) EMPTY (Holding OF (LIST (sp 2018 10 30 2022 10 30)), (LIST (sp 2018 10 30 2022 10 30))) (iso 2022 10 30) EMPTY)) EQUALS JUST 100000 -- S35 (d)(2): unmarried survivor, own 11 months, deceased spouse 4 years => deceased's period included => 100,000
#ASSERT gainOut (solo sale23 100000 (LIST (sp 2022 7 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2022 7 30 2023 6 30)) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 0 -- S36 (d)(2): survivor remarried, own 11 months only => 0, Guide: "if"

§ `Subsection (b)(5): nonqualified use (tolerance where days are counted)`

#ASSERT gainOut (solo (iso 2008 6 30) 200000 (LIST (sp 2000 1 1 2008 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2004 1 1 2008 6 30)) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 200000 -- S37 (b)(5)(C)(i): rental wholly before 2009-01-01 => no nonqualified use => 200,000
#ASSERT near (gainOut (solo (iso 2019 1 1) 200000 (LIST (sp 2009 1 1 2019 1 1)) (LIST (sp 2011 1 1 2019 1 1)) EMPTY)) 160000 500 -- S38 (b)(5): rental 2009-01-01 to 2011-01-01 counts, 2 of 10 years => 160,000 (+/- 500 for day count)  -- DIFFERS BY READING (lead, 2026-11-18), not noise: the reader's 160,000 counts whole years or months; the encoding's 160,032.85 counts (b)(5) ratio of nonqualified days to ownership days, spans inclusive of both ends, no rounding (forks F5, F9). With the reader's day count substituted in the inputs the same encoding returns exactly 160,000 (assertion P-S38 at the end of this file).
#ASSERT near (gainOut (solo (iso 2014 1 1) 140000 (LIST (sp 2007 1 1 2014 1 1)) (LIST (sp 2010 1 1 2014 1 1)) EMPTY)) 120000 500 -- S39 (b)(5)(C)(i): rental straddling 2009-01-01, only the 2009 year counts, 1 of 7 years => 120,000 (+/- 500)  -- DIFFERS BY READING (lead, 2026-11-18), not noise: the reader's 120,000 counts whole years or months; the encoding's 120,023.46 counts (b)(5) ratio in calendar days, spans inclusive (forks F5, F9). With the reader's day count substituted in the inputs the same encoding returns exactly 120,000 (assertion P-S39 at the end of this file).
#ASSERT gainOut (solo (iso 2021 12 31) 100000 (LIST (sp 2015 1 1 2021 12 31)) (LIST (sp 2015 1 1 2020 1 1)) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 100000 -- S40 (b)(5)(C)(ii)(I): vacant after the last use, inside the 5-year window => not nonqualified => 100,000
#ASSERT gainOut (soloT (iso 2023 1 1) 200000 (indSvc (LIST (sp 2010 1 1 2023 1 1)) (LIST (sp 2010 1 1 2012 12 31), (sp 2019 1 1 2023 1 1)) (LIST (uniSvc (sp 2013 1 1 2018 12 31) 200 FALSE)) FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS JUST 200000 -- S41 (b)(5)(C)(ii)(II): 6 years on qualified official extended duty => excepted => 200,000
#ASSERT gainOut (soloAbs (iso 2018 1 1) 160000 (LIST (sp 2010 1 1 2018 1 1)) (LIST (sp 2010 1 1 2011 12 31), (sp 2013 7 1 2018 1 1)) (absEmp (sp 2012 1 1 2013 6 30))) EQUALS JUST 160000 -- S42 (b)(5)(C)(ii)(III): 18 months away for a change of employment => excepted => 160,000
#ASSERT near (gainOut (soloAbs (iso 2018 1 1) 160000 (LIST (sp 2010 1 1 2018 1 1)) (LIST (sp 2010 1 1 2011 12 31), (sp 2014 7 1 2018 1 1)) (absEmp (sp 2012 1 1 2014 6 30)))) 150000 300 -- S43 (b)(5)(C)(ii)(III): 30 months away => 2 years excepted, 6 months nonqualified => 150,000 (+/- 300; the other reading gives 110,000)  -- DIFFERS BY READING (lead, 2026-11-18), not noise: the reader's 150,000 counts whole years or months; the encoding's 150,092.37 counts the 2-year absence cap counted as the days in the 2 calendar years ending on the sale, the ratio in calendar days (forks F10, F5, F9). With the reader's day count substituted in the inputs the same encoding returns exactly 150,000 (assertion P-S43 at the end of this file).
#ASSERT near (gainOut (solo (iso 2020 1 1) 150000 (LIST (sp 2010 1 1 2020 1 1)) (LIST (sp 2010 1 1 2013 12 31), (sp 2016 1 1 2020 1 1)) EMPTY)) 120000 500 -- S44 (b)(5)(C)(i): adult child lived there 2 years => 2 of 10 years nonqualified => 120,000 (+/- 500)  -- DIFFERS BY READING (lead, 2026-11-18), not noise: the reader's 120,000 counts whole years or months; the encoding's 120,024.64 counts (b)(5) ratio in calendar days, spans inclusive (forks F5, F9). With the reader's day count substituted in the inputs the same encoding returns exactly 120,000 (assertion P-S44 at the end of this file).
#ASSERT gainOut (soloSp (iso 2020 1 1) 150000 (LIST (sp 2010 1 1 2020 1 1)) (LIST (sp 2010 1 1 2013 12 31), (sp 2016 1 1 2020 1 1)) (LIST (sp 2014 1 1 2015 12 31))) EQUALS JUST 150000 -- S45 (b)(5)(C)(i): taxpayer's spouse lived there 2 years => no nonqualified use => 150,000
#ASSERT gainOut (soloSp (iso 2020 1 1) 150000 (LIST (sp 2010 1 1 2020 1 1)) (LIST (sp 2010 1 1 2013 12 31), (sp 2016 1 1 2020 1 1)) (LIST (sp 2014 1 1 2015 12 31))) EQUALS JUST 150000 -- S46 (b)(5)(C)(i): taxpayer's former spouse lived there 2 years => no nonqualified use => 150,000
#ASSERT gainOut (solo (iso 2019 1 1) 600000 (LIST (sp 2009 1 1 2019 1 1)) (LIST (sp 2011 1 1 2019 1 1)) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 250000 -- S47 (b)(5)+(b)(1): 120,000 allocated, remaining 480,000 capped at 250,000
#ASSERT near (gainOut (soloD (iso 2019 1 1) 200000 (LIST (sp 2009 1 1 2019 1 1)) (LIST (sp 2011 1 1 2019 1 1)) (dep 50000 (sp 2012 1 1 2015 12 31)))) 120000 500 -- S48 (b)(5)(D): (d)(6) first, then the 20 percent allocation on the other 150,000 => 120,000 (+/- 500)  -- DIFFERS BY READING (lead, 2026-11-18), not noise: the reader's 120,000 counts whole years or months; the encoding's 120,024.64 counts (b)(5) ratio in calendar days, after the (d)(6) allocation (forks F5, F9). With the reader's day count substituted in the inputs the same encoding returns exactly 120,000 (assertion P-S48 at the end of this file).

§ `Subsection (c): the reduced exclusion (tolerance where days are counted)`

#ASSERT near (gainOut (soloR sale23 200000 (LIST (sp 2022 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2022 6 30 2023 6 30)) EMPTY TRUE FALSE FALSE)) 125000 500 -- S49 (c): 1 year of use, change of employment, gain 200,000 => 125,000 (+/- 500)  -- DIFFERS BY READING (lead, 2026-11-18), not noise: the reader's 125,000 counts whole years or months; the encoding's 125,342.47 counts "1 year of use" counted as 366 days (both ends of 30 June to 30 June) over the 730 days of the 2 calendar years ending on the sale (forks F4, F5, F6). With the reader's day count substituted in the inputs the same encoding returns exactly 125,000 (assertion P-S49 at the end of this file).
#ASSERT gainOut (soloR sale23 100000 (LIST (sp 2022 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2022 6 30 2023 6 30)) EMPTY TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST 100000 -- S50 (c): same, gain 100,000 => 100,000
#ASSERT gainOut (soloR sale23 200000 (LIST (sp 2022 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2022 6 30 2023 6 30)) EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST 0 -- S51 (c)(2)(B): sold for a bigger house => 0, Guide: "if" in (c)(2)(B) unmet
#ASSERT near (gainOut (soloR sale23 200000 (LIST (sp 2022 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2022 6 30 2023 6 30)) EMPTY FALSE TRUE FALSE)) 125000 500 -- S52 (c): same, by reason of health => 125,000 (+/- 500)  -- DIFFERS BY READING (lead, 2026-11-18), not noise: the reader's 125,000 counts whole years or months; the encoding's 125,342.47 counts same as S49 (forks F4, F5, F6). With the reader's day count substituted in the inputs the same encoding returns exactly 125,000 (assertion P-S52 at the end of this file).
#ASSERT near (gainOut (soloR sale23 200000 (LIST (sp 2020 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (sp 2020 6 30 2023 6 30)) (LIST (iso 2022 6 30)) TRUE FALSE FALSE)) 125000 500 -- S54 (c)(1)(B)(II): 3 years of use but an earlier (a)-sale 1 year before => shorter period 1 year => 125,000 (+/- 500)  -- DIFFERS BY READING (lead, 2026-11-18), not noise: the reader's 125,000 counts whole years or months; the encoding's 124,657.53 counts the period between the two sales counted as the days strictly between them, 364 for 30 June to 30 June (fork F25). With the reader's day count substituted in the inputs the same encoding returns exactly 125,000 (assertion P-S54 at the end of this file).
#ASSERT (`s 121 the treatment of the gain from the sale or exchange` (soloR sale23 200000 base19 base19 EMPTY TRUE FALSE FALSE))'s `subsection (c) applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE -- S55 (c)(2)(A): (a) is met, so (c) does not apply => JUST FALSE, Guide: "if"

