§ `Reading probes: the eight near-boundary scenarios with the reader's day count substituted`

-- Each assertion below is the scenario above with dates shifted by a day or two so that the day counts equal the reader's whole-year counts (365 days to the year, 730 to two years).
-- The expected amounts are the reader's own, written before any module was opened; the encoding returns them exactly, so the differences above are differences of reading (calendar days against whole years), not of formula.

#ASSERT gainOut (solo (iso 2018 12 29) 200000 (LIST (sp 2009 1 1 2018 12 29)) (LIST (sp 2011 1 1 2018 12 29)) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 160000 -- P-S38
#ASSERT gainOut (soloD (iso 2018 12 29) 200000 (LIST (sp 2009 1 1 2018 12 29)) (LIST (sp 2011 1 1 2018 12 29)) (dep 50000 (sp 2012 1 1 2015 12 31))) EQUALS JUST 120000 -- P-S48
#ASSERT gainOut (solo (iso 2013 12 29) 140000 (LIST (sp 2007 1 1 2013 12 29)) (LIST (sp 2010 1 1 2013 12 29)) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 120000 -- P-S39
#ASSERT gainOut (solo (iso 2019 12 29) 150000 (LIST (sp 2010 1 1 2019 12 29)) (LIST (sp 2010 1 1 2013 12 31), (sp 2016 1 1 2019 12 29)) EMPTY) EQUALS JUST 120000 -- P-S44
#ASSERT gainOut (soloAbs (iso 2018 12 31) 160000 (LIST (sp 2010 1 8 2018 12 31)) (LIST (sp 2010 1 8 2011 12 31), (sp 2014 7 24 2018 12 31)) (absEmp (sp 2012 1 1 2014 7 23))) EQUALS JUST 150000 -- P-S43
